            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0414" n="406" xml:id="pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/2267: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-21T16:00:00+08:00">December 21, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 21—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1203. With reference to special train leaving December 23d, Japanese Consul
                    General informs me that details have been communicated to the Japanese military
                    and naval authorities in order that necessary arrangements may be made “not to
                    attack from the Japanese side, he said, train with about 300 foreigners on
                    board”.</p>
                <p>Sent to Hankow, repeated to the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
